course: dictionary
lesson: 905
title: Bivouac and camping words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bivouac is a simple, temporary camp, often made without a tent. Soldiers and mountain climbers may bivouac, which means to camp outside for the night in such a camp. The word can be a noun or a verb, so look at the sentence to see which one it is.
explain: Read the context to work out the meaning. «Army ants link their bodies into bridges and even a living nest called a bivouac, with no ant in charge.» The clues are «living nest» and «with no ant in charge»: the bivouac is a shelter that creatures build together, not a tent with someone in charge.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "a living nest called a simple, temporary camp". It still makes sense, so you are on the right track. When you are not sure, look the word up.
fact: A bivouac is a simple, temporary camp, often without a tent.
fact: To bivouac means to camp outside for the night in a simple camp.
fact: A bivvy, or bivvy bag, is a small waterproof shelter for one person.
fact: «Bivouac» can also mean a living nest, as in «a living nest called a bivouac» made by army ants.
fact: On outdoor trips, a bivouac can be made from branches or a tarp. Keep warm and dry, and never light a fire under a tarp.
exercise: «Army ants link their bodies into bridges and even a living nest called a bivouac.» What is a bivouac here? | *A simple, temporary shelter | A soldier who gives orders | A kind of ant food | A large bridge over a river
exercise: A bivvy bag is what? | A type of campfire | A kind of cooking pot | *A small waterproof shelter for one person | A large tent for a whole family
exercise: Soldiers will ___ in the field tonight before the battle. Which verb fits the gap? | tarp | *bivouac | kindle | bridge
test: In a story, soldiers bivouac in a field before a battle. What does bivouac mean here? | *To camp outside for the night in a simple camp | To sing a song | To make a bridge over a river | To run away quickly
test: Why should you never light a fire under a tarp when you bivouac? | Because a tarp needs to be dry before a fire | Because tarps are too cold to sit under | Because fire only works in a tent | *Because fire under a tarp can be dangerous to you and the shelter
exam: What is a bivvy? | A soldier's weapon | *A small waterproof shelter for one person | A large family tent | A kind of mountain bike
